ault, low-emphasis style used for common, non-critical actions."},"173":{"id":"/docs/components/button-24","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#critical","content":"The critical button signifies to the user a destructive action will take place."},"174":{"id":"/docs/components/button-25","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#disabled","content":"Any button variant can be disabled to prevent interaction, communicated with reduced opacity and a not-allowed cursor."},"175":{"id":"/docs/components/button-26","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#icon","content":"You may provide an optional `Icon` component to the button. Wrap the text beside an icon in a `Text`. If you do not include text, you must provide an aria-label attribute to identify the purpose of the button. This will produce a square button."},"176":{"id":"/docs/components/button-27","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#inline","content":"The inline button sits within a run of text, styled like a link while retaining button semantics."},"177":{"id":"/docs/components/button-28","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#minimal","content":"The minimal button is an icon-only button that's used when space is limited and/or when the action is universally understood."},"178":{"id":"/docs/components/button-29","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#sizes","content":"Buttons come in small, medium, and large sizes to fit different layout densities. Without\n`size`, a button follows the surrounding size scope, and uses medium outside any scope. An\nicon-only button is square and as tall as a text button of the same size."},"179":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"pag