ntrols; without it, the field follows the surrounding scope. An explicit `size` on a part still wins for that part"],[972,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, input, steppers, description, and error; without it, the field follows the surrounding scope"],[1333,"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets the label, trigger, and options, which open at the same size even though they render in a portal. Without it, the Select follows the surrounding scope"],[1722,"**Space / Enter**"],[1173,"**Space**: Select the focused radio button"],[294,"**Space**: Toggles the focused checkbox"],[879,"**Space/Enter**: activate an item; **Escape**: close"],[1298,"**Space/Enter**: Select the focused segment"],[721,"**Sprite Sheet Creation**: A hidden SVG sprite sheet is automatically injected into the DOM containing symbol definitions"],[731,"**SSR Limitation**: Sprite references render empty until client-side hydration"],[1389,"**Standalone** - with no parent context it renders with its own structural defaults and looks the same everywhere."],[971,"**Steppers**: A stepper is a `Group` holding `Button slot=\"decrement\"`, an `Input`, and `Button slot=\"increment\"`. Left empty, each button takes its icon and `variant=\"control\"` from the field, so no icon imports are needed. Compose a bare `Input` instead for a plain numeric input"],[1856,"**Sticky axes**: Positioned absolutely to remain visible during scroll"],[1845,"**Sticky y-axis**: The y-axis remains visible during horizontal scroll"],[671,"**Styling**: `className`, `style`, `data-*` attributes"],[715,"**SVG Parsing**: The fetched SVG string is parsed into a React element using `@bento/svg-parser`"],[1718,"**Tab**"],[293,"**Tab**: Moves focus to the next/previous checkbox"],[1170,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the radio group"],[1296,"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the segmented controller"],[1658,"**The body is `<Text slot=\"body\">`**, once or as many times as the copy needs."],[1656,"**The eyebrow is `slot=\"eyebrow\"`**, on either a `Text` or a `Tag`. The two forms swap\nfreely, and a `Tag` is sized to pair with the lockup."],[1657,"**The title is `<Heading slot=\"title\">`.** Pick the level from the document outline, not the\nvisual size: `size` handles the visuals, so `level={1}` in an `xs` lockup is perfectly valid."],[1125,"**Titles overflow:** that's expected — titles truncate. Shorten the title."],[1714,"**ToggleButton Item:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1713,"**ToggleButtonGroup Container:** `data-size`"],[1860,"**Tooltips** use absolute positioning and scroll-aware calculations for accurate placement"],[1849,"**Tooltips**: Show on both hover and focus for keyboard users"],[730,"**Trade-offs:**"],[672,"**Transform**: `rotate`, `flip` for icon transformations"],[486,"**Trigger and calendar**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a calendar icon and the formatted value from the field. `DatePickerCalendar` (and `DateRangePickerCalendar`) is the calendar in the popover it opens: it takes `Calendar` props plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `Calendar` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[1328,"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[882,"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"],[2036,"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."],[666,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1823,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[2100,"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."],[733,"**Use default mode** for SSR applications or when icons appear infrequently"],[734,"**Use sprite mode** when the same icons appear many times (navigation, lists, tables)"],[744,"**Use sprite mode**: For repeated icons, consider sprite mode which consolidates multiple icons into a single SVG sprite sheet, reducing DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[975,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1332,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1615,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[973,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[1878,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[1815,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[1854,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[1824,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[720,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[1446,"`--color-input-background-default`"],[1443,"`--color-input-background-selected`"],[1452,"`--color-input-text-default`"],[1453,"`--ux-1glcx6s`"],[1441,"`--ux-1m9ys0v`"],[1447,"`--ux-1nu8itt`"],[1450,"`--ux-1sbfig8`"],[1444,"`--ux-sywk25`"],[1456,"`--ux-zvaw3s`"],[203,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[2079,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2081,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2075,"`<Box orientation=\"horizontal\">`"],[2077,"`<Box orientation=\"vertical\">`"],[2082,"`<Flex alignItems=\"center\">`"],[2078,"`<Flex direction=\"column\" >`"],[2076,"`<Flex direction=\"row\" >`"],[2080,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[2032,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[602,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1651,"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."],[1176,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1301,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[403,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[296,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1177,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1302,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[298,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1179,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1730,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1303,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[402,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[1077,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[297,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1178,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[400,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1075,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1074,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"],[399,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[1076,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[401,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[2024,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[448,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[202,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[1835,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[282,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[352,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[370,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[348,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[363,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1772,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[439,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[449,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[450,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[441,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[1969,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1111,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[695,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[698,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[694,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[696,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[697,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[699,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1434,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[488,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[1584,"`Detail` is supporting copy, such as captions and metadata, on the detail ramp. It keeps the\nsurrounding color; add `emphasis=\"passive\"` to mute it."],[522,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[616,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1575,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1583,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[1005,"`Enter/Space`"],[60,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[446,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[564,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[789,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[531,"`Escape`"],[947,"`Escape`"],[1007,"`Escape`"],[1777,"`Escape`"],[601,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[2061,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[703,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[2099,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[618,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[453,"`Icon slot=\"indicator\"` is decorative and receives `aria-hidden=\"true\"` automatically."],[777,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[806,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[1952,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[619,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[2030,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[836,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[2029,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[871,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[200,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[491,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[940,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[935,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1110,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1827,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1503,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1767,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[797,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[780,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[999,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[783,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1049,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[1054,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1165,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[1971,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[1972,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[1970,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[949,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[1009,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[535,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[702,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[701,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[398,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1073,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1175,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1300,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1174,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1299,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1729,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1728,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[877,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1574,"`size` picks a step on the component's own ramp (`xs` to `2xl`) and changes only the font size."],[1649,"`size` sets every part, each on its own role ramp. Without it, the lockup follows the size\nscope."],[983,"`size` sets the label, input, and steppers. Without it, the field follows the surrounding size\nscope."],[1623,"`size` sets the label, input, description, and any control composed inside. Without it, the\nfield follows the surrounding size scope."],[503,"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."],[941,"`size` sets the modal's text, controls, and spacing. Without it, the modal follows the size\nscope around its trigger."],[617,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name, and takes the overlay's\ntitle tier, one step above the heading tier."],[2028,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[1356,"`sm`, `md`, or `lg` for the adopted components inside (listed below): their text, controls, and\ndefault spacing."],[95,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1460,"`Space` toggles t